        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.57,
            0.047,
            0.847,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "A Tale of Three Intersecting Lines"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.847,
            0.125
          ],
          "content": "How did you construct this triangle and what tools did you use? Can this construction be done only using a marked ruler (and a pencil)?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.125,
            0.849,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": "Constructing this triangle using just a ruler is certainly possible. But this might require several trials. Say we draw the base — let us call it AB — of length 4 cm (see the figure below), and mark the third point C using a ruler such that AC = 4 cm. This may not lead to BC also having a length of 4 cm. If this happens, we will have to keep making attempts to mark C till we get BC to be 4 cm long."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.383,
            0.246,
            0.615,
            0.429
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_1_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.442,
            0.653,
            0.465
          ],
          "content": "How do we make this construction more efficient?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.475,
            0.848,
            0.551
          ],
          "content": "Recall solving a similar problem in the previous year using a compass (in the Chapter ‘Playing with Constructions’). We had to mark the top point of a ‘house’ which is 5 cm from two other points. The method we used to get that point can also be used here."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.555,
            0.715,
            0.576
          ],
          "content": "After constructing $\\mathrm{AB} = 4$ cm, we can do the following."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.58,
            0.848,
            0.636
          ],
          "content": "**Step 1:** Using a compass, construct a sufficiently long arc of radius 4 cm from A, as shown in the figure. The point C is somewhere on this arc. How do we mark it?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.314,
